[{"id": "R001", "text": "The person stops the motor, listens to the hinge, and taps it while keeping the hatch closed. After the sound returns, they leave the hatch open and observe the motor wheel wobbling beside it."}, {"id": "R002", "text": "The person stops, adjusts the hatch slightly, then turns the motor off and runs it under a clean cover. If the noise returns, they stop and allow the machine to finish."}, {"id": "R003", "text": "The person taps the hatch, stops the motor, and pushes the hatch open with their palm. When the hatch opens slowly and air catches the seam, they move the motor one centimeter and leave the hatch open."}, {"id": "R004", "text": "The person stops the machine and photographs the contact ring, noting that the contact plate clicks against the housing while the motor moves slightly. They move the machine back and try again, then redirect their attention from the hatch to the motor."}, {"id": "R005", "text": "The person stops the machine, confirms the sound repeats, and rubs rust at the same location. They move the hatch closer while leaving the motor in place, and consider that the gear may be the source."}, {"id": "R006", "text": "The person stops the motor, rubs the hatch, scrapes rust from the bracket, and tries a new screw. They leave the old screw beside the old handle and leave the old drawer open."}, {"id": "R007", "text": "The person turns the hatch once, stops it before the door catches when the sound returns, and leaves the motor running. They mark the scrape location with a pencil."}, {"id": "R008", "text": "The person stops the hatch and listens, then moves it closer to the motor and taps the rust with a greasy fingertip. Although the sound remains associated with the hatch, they do not touch it further and consider the inspection complete."}, {"id": "R009", "text": "The person stops the motor, notes that their fingers are warm, and moves the hatch up before turning it over. They identify one bolt and leave the rust mark on the opposite side."}, {"id": "R010", "text": "The person reinstalls the hatch and restarts the machine, then attributes the rubbing to a loose screw and adjusts it. Because the screw shifts, they reinstall the hatch again and leave the machine running."}, {"id": "R011", "text": "The person turns the hatch handle, presses the screw once, lets the motor run briefly, and checks the screw again."}, {"id": "R012", "text": "The person moves the hatch toward the motor and presses it down with a pencil, after which the sound stops. They keep the pencil in place and leave the motor running until the next inspection."}]
